# Normalize line endings so the repo stops showing thousands of phantom
# modifications. Before this file existed, 2370 of 2928 tracked files were
# committed with CRLF and no core.autocrlf was set, so a checkout on any
# LF-normalizing tool produced a 206k-line diff hiding ~1k real changes.
#
# After adding this file, run once and commit the result on its own:
#   git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts: keep CRLF in the *working tree* for local edits.
# `text eol=crlf` normalizes the *blob* to LF — that breaks cmd.exe when users
# `curl` the file from raw.githubusercontent.com (GitHub serves the blob as-is).
# So install.bat must be stored with real CRLF bytes (-text = no conversion).
# PowerShell accepts LF, so install.ps1 can stay text/eol=crlf.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
scripts/install.bat -text

# Binary — never touch.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary

# Generated / vendored: keep out of language stats and collapse in diffs.
Cargo.lock          -diff linguist-generated
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES -diff linguist-generated
third_party/**      linguist-vendored
